# scripts/lib/protected_paths.list — protected deletion targets (constitution §11.4.287).
#
# Read at run time by scripts/lib/safe_rm.sh. The PreToolUse guard
# scripts/hooks/guard-destructive-paths.py does NOT read this file: it carries its own
# hardcoded, independent protected set (a superset of this list), and
# scripts/hooks/test_guard_bypasses.py fails if any entry here is missing from it (and if the
# guard fails to block any entry). Edit here for safe_rm.sh, and update the guard's sets too.
#
# FORMAT (one entry per line):
#   - Blank lines and lines whose first non-space character is '#' are ignored.
#   - Leading/trailing whitespace is trimmed. No inline comments.
#   - An entry starting with '/'  is an ABSOLUTE protected path. A delete target
#     whose fully resolved path (readlink -m) EQUALS it is refused. '/' itself is
#     refused by the consumer unconditionally and need not be listed.
#   - An entry starting with '~/' is a HOME-RELATIVE protected child. The part after
#     '~/' is a single path component, optionally a shell glob ('*', '?', '[...]'),
#     matched against the first component below every home directory the consumer
#     treats as a home ($HOME, SAFE_RM_EXTRA_HOMES). A target that resolves EXACTLY
#     to <home>/<matching component> is refused. Paths deeper inside it are not
#     refused by this list (e.g. <home>/Projects/app/build stays deletable).
#   - Any other line is a format error; consumers MUST fail closed on it.
# A consumer that cannot read this file, or finds no absolute entry in it, MUST
# refuse every delete (fail closed), never fall back to "nothing is protected".

# --- system directories (absolute) ---
/bin
/boot
/dev
/etc
/lib
/lib32
/lib64
/libx32
/opt
/proc
/root
/run
/sbin
/srv
/sys
/usr
/var
/mnt
/media
/snap
/home
/tmp
/Users

# --- home-relative protected children ---
~/scripts
~/Projects
~/.ssh
~/.gnupg
~/.claude*
~/.config
~/.local
~/vasic
~/ytdlp
~/backups
~/.cache
